1 NAME Mertayuda I R. Tumenggung
2 GIVN Mertayuda I
2 NSFX R. Tumenggung
1 NAME R. Tumenggung Mertayuda I
1 SEX M
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He was "Adipati" (king~sultan representative/ ruler/ commander) of Banyumas the IV 1620-1650
2 CONT
2 CONT Adipati rank  is equivalent as Duke in England /Europe
2 CONT
2 CONT ''''''More definition'''''' :
2 CONT From Malay adipati, 
2 CONT from Classical Malay اديڤتي (adipati, “king”), 
2 CONT from Javanese adipati 
2 CONT (ꦲꦢꦶꦥꦠꦶ, “king, queen; prince”), from Old Javanese 
2 CONT adhipati (“ruler; king”), 
2 CONT
2 CONT from Sanskrit अधिपति (adhipati, “ruler, king; commander”), compound of अधि (adhi) +‎ पति (pati).
2 CONT
2 CONT ''''''Other terminnology'''''':
2 CONT The title demang is a title for the leader of a region or area in ancient "Nusantara" (represent Indonesia in ancient era) society. [ 1 ] 
2 CONT
2 CONT Several individuals in history used this title, such as Demang "Lebar Daun" . 
2 CONT Its equivalent in Javanese culture is Adipati .
2 CONT
2 CONT In English, 
2 CONT the terms duke and duchess each derive from the French duc , which itself comes from the Latin dux , 'leader', a term used in republican Rome to refer to a military commander without formal rank (especially one of Germanic or Celt
2 CONC ic origin ), 
2 CONT
2 CONT and later to mean the chief military commander of a province. The title also has equivalents in various European languages.
